  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Slap and chase 1 v 1",
  "description": "Groups of three with one ball per basket (two groups can share a basket, one from each side). The three line up facing the basket. The middle player has the ball and attacks. The front player turns round and defends. The back player holds one arm out to the side.\n\nThe defender runs back and slaps the hand. As soon as the defender moves, the attacker drives to the basket and tries to score. The defender chases and tries to steal the ball or bother the finish. Rotate after every go: attacker becomes defender, defender holds the hand, and so on. Whoever is waiting cheers.\n\nVary it: hand closer/further away or high/low, or more space between the players. Play first to five, with a bonus point for a lay-up.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Attack: go at the basket straight away, at full speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Dribble with the hand furthest from the defender."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Defence: catch up, steal on the dribble or get your hands high on the finish."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "No fouls – no tackling from behind."
    }
  ],
